    wq#3548: add horus to the legacy SSH fallback map

    manifest_add_node's documented step 2 (add the new node to storage_probe's
    SSH map) was skipped on the 2026-10-07 04:43Z horus add. storage_probe's
    primary resolution path is the fleet inventory, which already carries horus
    (network.ssh.user/tailscale_ip), but the SSH_FALLBACK dict this inventory
    lookup falls back to on a transient resolution failure had no horus entry,
    so the one blip during the wq#3537 overlay-drift remediation window
    (concurrent apply_overlay.py --apply writes around 07:24-07:25Z) surfaced as
    "no ssh mapping (inventory + legacy)" instead of transparently failing over.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

